  "body": "## What changed\n\n- consolidates the canonical resident runtime, grounded claim/evidence firewall, provider receipts, Prime-VCW conversation recovery, and typed Body request/proof lane\n- completes native/Qt/CMake/Rust coverage semantics, lifecycle authorization/migration/resume/rebind, germ v2, metabolic governance, bounded resource offers, face attestations, lineage, and ancestor queries\n- migrates a distinct NotepadNext Mantle 2 candidate while preserving historical evidence\n- closes all 98 correction rows and 25 recorded friction events with executable evidence\n- adds Windows contract CI, package build/install validation, release manifests, and content scans\n\n## Why\n\nMantleOS 2.0 needs one shared, evidence-grounded platform contract rather than example-specific resident dialects and partially wired lifecycle/security interfaces.\n\n## Compatibility and security impact\n\n- breaking: Mantle 2 activation accepts `mantle-germ-v2`; legacy artifacts require explicit inert migration\n- maintained residents must declare `mantle-resident-v2`\n- external hatch/graft requires fresh target-bound authorization; MIND fusion remains separately dual-authorized\n- historical certification is never treated as current runtime authority\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python -m mantle prove`: 148/148 PASS\n- `python -m mantle check --strict --json`: 14/14 PASS, 0 skipped\n- full pytest: 90 passed, 2 declared skips, 3 subtests\n- NotepadNext lifecycle audit v2: PASS; distinct genesis keys; historical hashes unchanged\n- wheel/sdist build, Twine validation, clean offline wheel install: PASS\n- Organize.AppAI: 299 passed, 4 declared skips; end-to-end demo PASS on Mantle 2; fresh application certification PASS\n- release/private-path scan: PASS\n",
